description:
NexusShared/Models/SpecSummary.swift:59 has a malformed conditional binding:

  if let s = try? c.decodeIfPresent(String.self, forKey: .lastModified), let s {

decodeIfPresent already returns String? (optional). 'try?' wraps another optional layer making it String??. The first 'let s' unwraps to String?, then 'let s {' is a syntax shadow that doesn't actually unwrap further — compiler reports: 'initializer for conditional binding must have Optional type, not String'.

This bug was MASKED by the nx-jmqyk silent-drop bug since 2026-05-17 (Models/ subdir was excluded from NexusShared.framework compilation). nx-jmqyk fix exposed it 2026-05-18.

Fix is one of:
  if let s = try c.decodeIfPresent(String.self, forKey: .lastModified) {
or:
  if case let s?? = try? c.decodeIfPresent(String.self, forKey: .lastModified) {

Blocks NexusShared compilation on all platforms.

During nx-d40qb (resolve 32 TS errors), the agent confirmed 27 pre-existing test failures in apps/agent/src/notifications and apps/agent/src/services tests. Failures are RUNTIME (not type) — orthogonal to the TS errors that nx-d40qb fixed.

Root causes per agent's report:
1. SyntaxError: missing export 'narrowSessionStatus' — somewhere a barrel/index expects it but no source exports it. Need to either add the export OR fix consumers to use the canonical narrowing helper.
2. Audio business logic failures in manager.audio.test.ts (2 cases) — likely pre-spine-migration drift; assertions don't match current notification.audioBase64 handling (Swift owns synth now).

Verified identical pre/post-fix failure count via stash check during nx-d40qb. NOT introduced by recent work.

